  "generalNotes": [
    "Bracket 'min' values are the income level at which that marginal rate begins; brackets are applied progressively.",
    "Head-of-household brackets are not separately published by most states in the Tax Foundation dataset; where a state does not define its own HoH schedule, the 'single' schedule is used as a standard industry approximation. This is flagged per-state via 'hohUsesSingleBrackets'.",
    "'exemptionType': 'deduction' amounts reduce taxable income; 'credit' amounts reduce tax liability dollar-for-dollar (modeled in state.ts accordingly).",
    "specialPayrollTax entries represent additional employee-side payroll withholdings (SDI / PFL / FAMLI / long-term-care) that are NOT part of the state income tax but materially affect net pay. Entries marked 'verified: false' use the most recent confirmed rate available and should be reviewed each January when states publish new figures.",
    "Local/county income taxes (e.g., in MD, NY-NYC/Yonkers, OH, PA, IN, IA, KY) are out of scope for Phase 1 and are handled by a future localTax.ts module."
  ],
